dam Fantilli","shortName":"A. Fantilli"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4565244","displayName":"Simon Holmstrom","shortName":"S. Holmstrom"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"7226","fullName":"UBS Arena","address":{"city":"Elmont","state":"NY","zipCode":"11003","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/7226.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":14295,"officials":[{"fullName":"Cody Beach","displayName":"Cody Beach","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Matt MacPherson","displayName":"Matt MacPherson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kendrick Nicholson","displayName":"Kendrick Nicholson","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Shawn Oliver","displayName":"Shawn Oliver","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Defenseman Matthew Schaefer records 1st NHL hat trick as Islanders beat Columbus 5-1","description":"— Defenseman Matthew Schaefer recorded his first NHL hat trick and Anthony Duclair had a goal and an assist as the New York Islanders beat the Columbus Blue Jackets 5-1 on Tuesday night.","story":"NEW YORK -- — Defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291933/matthew-schaefer\">Matthew Schaefer</a> recorded his first NHL hat trick and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042086/anthony-duclair\">Anthony Duclair</a> had a goal and an assist as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyi/new-york-islanders\">New York Islanders</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cbj/columbus-blue-jackets\">Columbus Blue Jackets</a> 5-1 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Schaefer became the second-youngest defenseman in NHL history to record a hat trick. Only Hall of Famer Phil Housley at 18 years, 320 days was younger than Schaefer at 19 years, 73 days. Schaefer joined Housley as the only players at the position to reach 30 goals before age 20.\n\n\r\n              The 19-year-old Schaefer opened his scoring 1:34 into the second period. He scored twice in the third, at 7:01 off assists from Duclair and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042019/ryan-pulock\">Ryan Pulock</a>, and capped his night by scoring his ninth goal of the season into an empty net with 3:52 remaining.\n\n\r\n              Schaefer’s hat trick first by an Islanders' defenseman since Denis Potvin in 1982.\n\n\r\n              Anthony DeAngelo also scored for the Islanders, who won their third straight game after a four-game skid. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3151981/ilya-sorokin\">Ilya Sorokin</a> finished with 28 saves.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899972/zach-werenski\">Zach Werenski</a> spoiled Sorokin's bid for a shutout with a goal 1:12 into the third period. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5734/cam-talbot\">Cam Talbot</a> had 36 saves for the Blue Jackets, who lost their fifth straight game and for the seventh time in nine games.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blue Jackets: At the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/chi/chicago-blackhawks\">Chicago Blackhawks</a> on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Islanders: At the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/wpg/winnipeg-jets\">Winnipeg Jets</a> on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              The Associated Press created this story using technology provided by <a href=\"https://www.dataskrive.com/\">Data Skrive</a> and data from <a href=\"https://www.sportradar.com/\">Sportradar</a>.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-18T15:12:23Z"}}